{"id": "EUVD-2026-98937", "enisaUuid": "4acf2b86-01b9-3e78-97aa-6879b193a608", "description": "Xxyopen novel through 3.5.0 contains a weak password hashing vulnerability that allows attackers to recover plaintext passwords because UserServiceImpl.register() stores unsalted MD5 digests in user_info.password. Attackers who obtain the password column through a database leak or backup exposure can crack hashes with precomputed tables or GPU brute force and reuse credentials.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T16:53:07", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T17:22:41", "baseScore": 8.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/201206030/novel/pull/53", "https://github.com/201206030/novel/blob/v3.5.0/src/main/java/io/github/xxyopen/novel/service/impl/UserServiceImpl.java#L70-L77", "https://github.com/201206030/novel/commit/fa82ce7e426a5b29db469b8f13d2e29fc1260871", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/novel-through-3.5.0-unsalted-md5-password-storage"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110104", "GHSA-25gx-36j3-jw66"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.28, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a1f71048-fbfc-35d2-bbe9-c251f3d9b017", "product": {"name": "Novel", "vendor": {"name": "201206030"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.5.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6af1d48d-0184-3ccf-897e-6d93063b98ed", "vendor": {"name": "xxyopen"}}], "isExploited": false}